## 15. HTTP API catalog (backend)

Authoritative routing is implemented in `src/backend/server.ts`. Requests normalize the URL by stripping leading duplicate slashes (e.g. `//generate-tests` → `/generate-tests`).

| Method | Path | Auth | Notes |
|--------|------|------|------|
| POST | `/generate-tests` | Yes | JSON: `prId`, `projectName`, `repositoryId`; optional `customContext` (max **3000** characters enforced server-side before AI). Returns `title`, `htmlDescription`, `sourceCommitId`, `targetCommitId`, optional `compressionReport`. |
| POST | `/create-work-item` | Yes | Requires `testCase`, `prId`, `projectName`, `repositoryId`, `projectId`, `sourceCommitId`, `targetCommitId`. |
| POST | `/post-pr-comment` | Yes | `workItemId` may be omitted when `commentContent` is provided (full-output / custom comment path). |
| POST | `/api/extract-purpose-scope` | Yes | Body: `{ "html": string }` → `{ "extracted": string }` via `ai.extractPurposeAndScope`. |
| POST | `/api/queue/pr` | Yes (+ active license when `ENABLE_LICENSE_ENFORCEMENT`) | Redis enqueue; **503** if `UPSTASH_REDIS_*` missing (`MissingEnvironmentVariableError`). |
| GET | `/license/status` | Yes | Rate limit then auth (handler not wrapped in `applyMiddleware` — follow existing pattern when adding similar routes). |
| POST | `/license/activate` | Yes | Content-Type JSON; body read in router then passed to `licenseRoutes.handleLicenseActivate`. |
| POST | `/webhooks/lemon-squeezy` | **Public** (verified inside handler) | Rate limited; raw body string for signature verification. |
| GET/HEAD | `/health`, `/` | Public | Uptime + timestamp only — do not reintroduce internal queue stats. |

**Commented / inactive (do not re-enable piecemeal)**: `POST /webhook`, `POST /api/webhook-token`, and `queue.startWorker()` from `src/backend/queue.ts` — see repeated architecture comments in `server.ts` (OAuth token lifetime, no frontend token push).

---

## 16. Two queue systems (do not conflate)

1. **`src/backend/queue.ts`** — In-memory array + `worker()` loop: `addJob`, `processJob`, `fetchWithRetry`, used only by the **disabled** service-webhook design. **Not** started unless `queue.startWorker()` is uncommented alongside the full token-store pipeline.
2. **Redis path** — `enqueue.ts` / `dequeue.ts` / `worker/worker.ts` + **`POST /api/queue/pr`**: durable jobs, `validateQueueEnvironment()` for `UPSTASH_REDIS_URL` and `UPSTASH_REDIS_TOKEN`.

When designing or reviewing changes, name which queue you mean. Never treat “enqueue” as interchangeable without an explicit migration plan.

---

## 17. CORS (`applyCorsHeaders` in `server.ts`)

- **Missing `Origin`**: respond with `Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *` and **`Access-Control-Allow-Credentials: false`** (log line treats as server-to-server / non-browser CORS client).
- **Present `Origin`**: must match an allowlist pattern (Azure DevOps hosts, `*.visualstudio.com`, gallery CDN, legacy app hostnames in code, etc.). The API itself is deployed on **Render** in production; browser calls from the extension still originate from **Azure DevOps** origins, not `*.onrender.com`, unless you add pages or tools that call the API from another site—then extend `basePatterns` accordingly. In **`NODE_ENV === "development"`**, localhost, optional ngrok host, and `process.env.NGROK_URL` may be appended — keep dev entries minimal and never widen production patterns casually.
- **Allowed headers** (exposed to browsers): include **`Authorization`** and **`X-Ado-Org-Url`**. If the extension sends new custom headers, update this list and the extension’s `fetch` in the same change.

---

## 18. AI prompt contract (`system-prompt.txt` + `src/backend/ai.ts`)

- **Load path**: `loadSystemPrompt()` reads **`path.join(process.cwd(), 'system-prompt.txt')`**. Build copies the file into `dist/` and `dist/backend/` — production working directory must still resolve this path or startup fails (`process.exit` in `ai.ts` on read error).
- **Model output**: JSON with **`title`** and **`htmlDescription`** only; Gemini `responseSchema` enforces that shape. HTML must follow the **11-section** contract and tag whitelist in `system-prompt.txt`.
- **Short prompt on retry**: `OPTIONAL_SHORT_PROMPT_HEADINGS` in `ai.ts` strips optional blocks by **exact heading substring** match. If you edit headings in `system-prompt.txt`, update `ai.ts` in lockstep or retry behavior silently stops shortening the system prompt.
- **Compression**: `buildUserPrompt` / `buildUserPromptWithTokenCap` and `diff-config.ts` define token/line budgets — changing limits affects observability fields (`COMPRESSION_SUMMARY`, `sectionsRemoved`) and test expectations.
- **Legacy**: `htmlDescriptionBase64` decode path exists for backward compatibility — do not reintroduce for new clients.

---

## 19. ADO client (`src/backend/ado-client.ts`) conventions

- Use **`azdev.getBearerHandler(token)`** + `WebApi(orgUrl, authHandler)` for extension OAuth tokens.
- Work items are **`Task`** work item type with `System.Tags` **`AI-Generated`** or **`AI-Generated-Fallback`**.
- **`sanitizeHTML`** wraps AI- or user-influenced HTML for `System.Description` and PR comments; always pass a distinct **`source`** string for log/traceability (`ado.createTaskWorkItem`, `ado.postPRComment`, etc.).
- **PR linking**: `buildPRArtifactUri` → `vstfs:///Git/PullRequestId/...` artifact relation on create.
- **Diff helpers**: `generateUnifiedDiff`, `generateSyntheticFileDiff`, iteration paging — keep `diff-config.ts` imports and caps coherent when tuning AI context.

---

## 20. Extension license API (`src/license/api.ts`)

- Obtains token via **`SDK.getAccessToken()`** and org base URL via **`ILocationService.getServiceLocation(undefined, undefined)`** (same pattern as `backendClient.ts`).
- **`getLicenseStatus(baseUrl, signal?)`**: GET `/license/status` with Bearer + `X-Ado-Org-Url`; supports **`AbortSignal`**.
- **`activateLicense`**: POST JSON with trimmed **`licenseKey`**, **`organization`**, **`userId`** from `SDK.getUser()`.
- **`buildUrl`**: rejects non-`http` schemes — align any new client helpers with **`backendClient`’s** stricter absolute-URL validation where appropriate.

---

## 21. Webhook URL policy (`src/services/configService.ts`)

- **`WEBHOOK_ENDPOINT`** is **fixed** to `https://api.qazent.com/webhook` — subscription UIs must not allow arbitrary user-defined webhook URLs (see file header).
- **Server reality**: `POST /webhook` handling is **commented out** in `server.ts`. Any future re-enable must align this constant, infrastructure, ADO service hook registration, and the encrypted token / org store design — do not assume the live server already accepts that URL.

---

## 22. When uncertain

- Read the file or run the script; do not guess paths, env var names, or endpoint shapes.
- If a required doc or env template is missing from the workspace (e.g. `.env.example` referenced in README but absent), state the gap and ask for the artifact rather than inventing values.

